Z||000000||Tina||06-25-2001||11:07 PM||||Perhaps the problem I got is absolutly normal,and I should just get used to it.<BR>But this the first T-Top I ever owned, so Iam not really familiar with it.<BR>Here it goes.<BR>When ever I wash the car, water gets trapped<BR>inside the doorseal attached to the glass.<BR>(Yes, I've already learned.Take 'em out,tip,drain,and then drive out of the bay)<P>Is there something wrong with the seal itself?<BR>Did install new seals myself. Did I miss a step?<BR>A closeup pic of the seal with the window all the way up would really help.<P>That, or a "Get used to it Tina"<P>Thanks,<BR>Tina  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-26-2001||04:49 AM||||Tina--Feel free to drop off your Ttops (along with the rest of the roof) to me and I'll be sure to investigate fully.  Of course, I'll have to do some 'real world' testing (by installing them on <I>my</I> car).  Email me so we can make delivery arrangements.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000002||RossT||06-26-2001||05:04 AM||||Be more specific and I will e-mail you several pics.<P>Sounds like your door gass needs to be adjusted up, or your t-top glass can be adjusted down slightly to make a better glass<BR>seal between the top of the glass and the glass weatherseal.<P>could also be that water is getting in thru the end caps.<P>Read the waterleak manual at <A HREF="http://www.fierottop.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fierottop.com</A> <P>If you still need pics, then let me know<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||artherd||06-26-2001||05:10 AM||||Hi Tina!  I've found the same thing, the babies will leak if you put high pressure water on them.<P>Solution, wash t-top cars at home  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>PS: where exactly is your leak? mine leak a bit where the window seals to the wetherstriping, but the ttop itself is very well sealed.<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000004||Tina||06-26-2001||07:38 PM||||O.K, acording to the  "Leak manual" (Thanks, RossT)it should be a T-roof glass panel leak.<BR>Symtoms are right.<BR> Water filling<BR>                 the inside of the<BR>                 latch cover or<BR>                 along the rail<BR>                 weatherseal.<BR>Only a reseal is required to fix that problem.<BR>But you tell me, does this look right?<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1315468&a=12269353&p=50966377"> <BR>Got my doubts there,especially the way the middle of the seal get's pulled down from the window glass<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">Tina <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||qwikgta||06-26-2001||09:22 PM||||Tina, send pic of your dash, it looks like you have done something to the gauges or is just the angle of the pic.<P>Rob<P>------------------<BR>qwikgta@yahoo.com<BR>88 T-Top coupe, 65K, Header no Cat, 16" GTZ rims, short shifter, swaybar, open element air cleaner, hood vents.<BR>http://robsfieroproject.homestead.com/index.html<BR>http://vafiero.com||||reg||1
Z||000006||Phil||06-26-2001||09:36 PM||||I'm new to ttops myself but it looks like you're missing a piece-the drip edge. It's a rubber/vinyl strip about 1"wide that is glued into the small recess in the metal piece just above the the rubber window seal.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tina||06-26-2001||10:00 PM||||Wouldn't you know it.<BR>Neither of my 2 T's has these things on there.<BR>Thanks for solving that mystery for me.<P>Tina<BR>Oh, almost forgot the dash.<BR>Here you go qwikgta/Rob<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=1315468&a=12269353&p=50116038"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000008||perks88gt||06-27-2001||01:11 AM||||Digressing on the topic, those dash picks look bad ass, where did you get them, or create them?  Anyway back to the matter at hand, t-tops leak.  Fact.  Mine leaked even at home with the "low" pressure washer.  You pic of your tops does not show enough.  Is the felt "wind gaurd" ripped"  My t-tops always leaked when i put direct spray to them, even if it was a squirt gun.  I love t-tops, but they were not meant to be with the fiero||||reg||1
